{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01262 - MONDO_17893",
  "verbalization": "Decitabine is associated with Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a series of indirect pathways, primarily through its indication for Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation and Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome. These conditions are linked to Ivosidenib, which in turn is indicated for Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The evidence suggests that Decitabine may exert a therapeutic effect on a subset of leukemias, potentially through mechanisms that involve the modulation of DNA methylation or other epigenetic processes. The overlapping indications and the shared target of Ivosidenib imply a possible mechanistic link between Decitabine and the development or progression of Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Decitabine in the treatment of a broader spectrum of leukemias, with the potential for repurposing in inherited forms of the disease.",
